    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The only test class is `AcceptanceTest`, and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` behavior with minimal structural impact by concentrating the new logic in the small, cohesive `HouseholdDuplicates` helper rather than growing the large controller or entity.\n\n**Behavior:** When a request sets `sharesHousehold: true` and the new owner matches an existing same-last-name owner at the same address, the create is allowed (existing rule) and the owner is stamped with a stable, shared `householdId`. The id is a deterministic SHA\u2011256 digest of the normalized `lastName + address`, so every owner in the same household derives the identical value \u2014 no cross-owner mutation or re-saving is needed, and it's returned on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `HouseholdDuplicates.java` (small helper, low surrounding complexity) \u2014 added `assignHousehold(...)` and a private `householdId(key)` deriving the stable id. Reuses the existing `key`/`norm` logic.\n- `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` \u2014 a **single** added line calling `HouseholdDuplicates.assignHousehold(...)`, keeping the change to this large class to one line.\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added the `householdId` field with a plain getter/setter (each CC=1) and `@Column`.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added `householdId` as a read-only field on the `Owner` response schema (MapStruct maps it by name automatically).\n- `db/hsqldb/schema.sql` + `data.sql` \u2014 added the `household_id` column and the matching positional value in the seed inserts (the hsqldb schema is the one the tests use and the only one kept in sync).",
